# Cursor Rule File for Full-Stack Applications

## Framework and Language
- Use Next.js for the frontend framework.
- Use TypeScript for type safety and data consistency.
- Use Supabase for backend operations, including database and storage.

## State Management and Data Fetching
- Use TanStack Query for all data fetching and mutations to ensure automatic caching and efficient state management.
- Set `staleTime` and `gcTime` for queries to balance freshness and performance, e.g., 5 minutes for `staleTime`.
- Invalidate queries after mutations using `queryClient.invalidateQueries` to maintain data consistency.

## Performance Optimizations
- Use Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR) for static pages, setting `revalidate` to update periodically, e.g., every 60 seconds.
- Implement caching for API routes using `cache` from React to reduce server load.
- Lazy load components using `dynamic` import to reduce initial bundle size and improve load times.
- Use server-side rendering (SSR) for pages requiring real-time data to ensure fresh content.

## Framework Version
- Ensure the project uses the latest stable version of Next.js, currently 14.2.3 as of March 5, 2025.
- Check compatibility with React 18 and other dependencies before upgrading.
- Test thoroughly after updating to ensure no breaking changes.

## Code Structure
- Maintain a clear structure with services, utilities, and UI components for separation of concerns.
- Use centralized error handling with user feedback via toasts for consistency.

## Security
- Use Supabase Row Level Security (RLS) for access control to protect sensitive data.
